{
  "name": "Marketing — WhatsApp Broadcasts (WATI)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WhatsApp broadcasts (WATI)\n**Campaigns sheet → opted-in Customers → WATI template broadcast.**\n\n1. Add a row to `Campaigns` with `channel=whatsapp`, an **approved** WATI `template_name`, `segment` (all | vip | regular | new | lapsed | birthday) and `send_at`, then set `status=approved`.\n2. Every 15 min the oldest due campaign is locked (`processing`), the audience is built (opt-in, not opted out, frequency cap), and sent in chunks of 100.\n3. Results are written back to `Campaigns`, `MarketingLog` and `Customers.last_promo_at`.\n\n`template_params` is JSON, e.g. `[{\"name\":\"name\",\"value\":\"{first_name}\"},{\"name\":\"offer\",\"value\":\"{offer}\"}]`. Tokens: `{first_name} {name} {offer} {business_name}`.\n\n**Inbound webhook:** point WATI → Webhooks → *Message Received* at `/webhook/wati-inbound`. STOP / START update consent.",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "e6cf54d1-9bec-4dc0-b496-ec1c70d6c0a7",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -480,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "minutes",
              "minutesInterval": 15
            }
          ]
        }
      },
